    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "The unprotected sweep() function was exploited. Vulnerable code snippet: https://www.oklink.com/es-la/bsc/address/0x8cf0a553ab3896e4832ebcc519a7a60828ab5740/contract Attack tx: https://www.oklink.com/es-la/bsc/tx/0xd423ae0e95e9d6c8a89dcfed243573867e4aad29ee99a9055728cbbe0a523439 https://explorer.phalcon.xyz/tx/bsc/0xd423ae0e95e9d6c8a89dcfed243573867e4aad29ee99a9055728cbbe0a523439 https://app.blocksec.com/explorer/tx/bsc/0x7ccb189c78376bdc35294f1779e7156233bcbc65f8681b3d6a7f512c1c2d5218 Analysis: // Unprotected function here. Call to sweep will rise WBNB price Elephant.sweep(); https://x.com/Phalcon_xyz/status/1732354930529435940"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "ElephantStatus on BNB Chain was exploited on December 6, 2023, when an attacker used spot price manipulation to drain approximately $165,000 by abusing the protocol’s unprotected sweep() function. The sweep() function in the ElephantStatus contract was callable without adequate protection, allowing the attacker to manipulate token prices via flash loans and AMM swaps. The contract relied on manipulable spot prices, creating an exploitable oracle weakness."
    }
  ],
